			"notes": "#### Completed the port to NeoForge for Minecraft versions >=1.21.9\n- The jars support 1.21, 1.21.1, 1.21.9, 1.21.10 and 1.21.11.\n- The fabric jars support 1.21.x.\n- Neoforge 1.21.11 does not use parchment.\n\n#### Backported NeoForge to 1.21, 1.21.1.\n#### Backported Fabric to 1.21-1.21.8.\n\n# Major Core Code Changes\n- Started preparing for dropped Yarn support in Minecraft 26.1.\n- Transitioned from Yarn mappings to official Mojang mappings.\n### Disclaimer for mod developers\n- This build also changes the API to use GuiGraphics instead of DrawContext which may break mod compatibility for 1.21.9 onwards as this build supports 1.21.1,1.21.9, 1.21.10 and 1.21.11. Mods will need changes to successfully hook into the API again. Disclaimer: A v2 API will be released sometime in the development of 5.x.x of the mod, ETA: Planned - 26.2 | Min - 26.1 | Max- 26.3\n- The 1.21 and 1.21.1 build will need additional support in mods that are using the redlime mod right now.\n\n# Gameplay/Mod Changes\n- Added configurable armor durability notifications.\n- Added basic armor trim overlay.\n- Made the trim rendering dynamic.\n- Added resource reload listener to refresh texture caches when resource packs change.\n- Allowed using the same mod file for 1.21.9, 1.21.10 and 1.21.11.\n- Backported to 1.21.1."
		},
